# NSG fix: RRU.PrbUsedDl zeroed out in high-MCS / light-load regimes
#
# Reference note (distro trees are the source of truth; build-slim.sh bakes
# them). One file pair changes:
#   contrib/oran-interface/helper/mmwave-indication-message-helper.{h,cc}
#
# ── Symptom ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A buildings run measured DL 8.9 Mbps/UE with RRU.PrbUsedDl mean 0.0 —
# physically impossible (you cannot carry throughput on zero PRBs).
# Intermittent: the same config later reported sane values (5-13 per UE).
#
# ── Root cause: a double truncation that defeats its own ceil ────────────────
# The caller (mmwave-enb-net-device.cc, BuildRicIndicationMessageDu) computes
# the per-UE PRB average as a fractional double:
#     macPrb = macNumberOfSymbols / denominatorPrb * 139;
# and passes it to AddDuUePmItem — whose parameter was **long**, so the
# fraction was truncated AT THE CALL BOUNDARY. The body then does
#     ueVal->AddItem<long> ("RRU.PrbUsedDl.UEID", (long) std::ceil (macPrb));
# i.e. the author intended to round the fraction UP — but ceil never sees a
# fraction, because it already died in the parameter. Any UE whose per-window
# PRB average fell below 1 (exactly the high-MCS regime buildings create, or
# any light-load cell) reported 0; with every UE below 1, the whole metric
# read 0.0. Whether a given run trips it depends on the report-window timing,
# hence the intermittence.
#
# ── Fix ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The macPrb parameter is now double (header + impl); the existing
# (long) std::ceil (macPrb) finally does what it was written to do. Values
# shift up by <1 PRB (5->6, 12->13 observed) — the intended ceil semantics.
# Callers already passed a double, so no call-site changes; long arguments
# from other callers widen implicitly.
#
# NOTE: signature changes in a shared lib require rebuilding EVERYTHING that
# links it — a hot docker-cp of only the changed .so left the old scenario
# binary calling a mangled symbol that no longer existed and the run died as
# "partial". Always ./ns3 build + build-slim + container restart.
#
# ── Verified (2026-07-16) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Buildings run after fix: SINR 24.9 dB, DL 8.76 Mbps/UE, PRB 7.6 (per-UE
# 6-14). Permanent regression guard in tools/fidelity_report.py:
# "L4 PRB consistency — thp > 0 requires PRB > 0".
